In article <dsnoek.3gn6@terapin.com> dsnoek@terapin.com (Daniel Snoek) writes:
>How do I tell which god I'm aligned to so I don't piss him off when I
>offer at a temple?

Offering doesn't work like that.  When you offer a sacrifice at an
altar that isn't consecrated to your deity, your god will attempt to
re-consecrate the altar in his/her name.  If you fail to convert the
altar, then your god will get annoyed.  The way you can tell which
deity the altar is dedicated to is by looking at it. ('/')


